          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "داروغہ — dāroghā — \"a police inspector\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "داروغہ تھانے میں نہیں تھا۔ dāroghā thāne meṅ nahīṅ thā. The inspector was not at the police station."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is usually traced to Persian dārogha, \"an overseer\", a word Persian is thought to have taken from Mongolian. In a town the داروغہ (dāroghā) runs the تھانہ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
